comments[16]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-04T18:26:03.448Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: searched restore from history, zero-byte item, corrupted stream tail, missing item file recovery. The closed v2026.5.1 restore-recovery lineage (linked recurs_from) covered absent files only. Reproduced live on the 2026.9.4 build in a sandbox tracker before filing: three verified history entries, zero-byte item file, get and restore both refuse with the TOON shape error."
  "2026-09-04T19:42:55.221Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope combines verified restoration, invalid-tail salvage, stable addresses, identity reservation, and replay-gate evidence with pm-m0yjtg, pm-qw1uw6, pm-e3gn0z, and pm-wlqxg3. GitHub issue 1171 already links this canonical owner. No duplicate item created."
  "2026-09-04T20:00:51.081Z","harness:codex","Safety contract: salvage is a separate explicit single-stream repair mode, refuses parseable interior records and potentially complete records with attached corruption, preserves verified prefix bytes and hash epoch, binds ownership to a readable current item or verified replay, rechecks snapshots under lock and appends a suffix-digest receipt. It does not normalize provenance or reconcile current state."
  "2026-09-04T21:05:43.648Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: Recover unreadable UTF-8 item documents from verified history and salvage only an invalid trailing suffix with byte-preserving audit receipts and concurrency guards. The recovery and negative-control integration fixtures passed; temporary-tracker acceptance confirmed byte-identical restoration, unchanged dry-run bytes, retained-prefix bytes and suffix digest. Windows execution remains a required hosted check before merge. Repository-wide exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and pnpm quality:static passed without weakening thresholds. All changed surfaces are linked to canonical delivery items. Hosted PR review and merged-main operational verification are pending and must pass before merge; the already published 2026.9.4 artifact does not contain this branch."
  "2026-09-04T21:08:55.655Z","harness:codex","Pre-merge verification gap: the existing Windows job selects an explicit suite and does not automatically run new integration files. Add history-durability and history-maintenance-replay to the required job; Linux coverage already passed, but no Windows recovery success is claimed until that exact hosted job completes."
  "2026-09-04T21:09:24.294Z","harness:codex","Review surface: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1194 at initial implementation head 4c80eb3b6d4d5c52deee2b1bcd0e53f074414c27. Final frozen repository validation passed with 2637 items, 2652 history streams, zero drift or storage-integrity failures. Existing 295 historical resolution gaps remain documented on pm-e9zh; they are not repaired with placeholder metadata."
  "2026-09-04T21:11:45.608Z","harness:codex","Additional final checks passed: required defect-evidence gate (122 governed terminal defects, 8 recurrence families, zero findings), context-quality and 55 token surfaces, packed npm/npx/bunx smoke with 13 packages, and package-first dogfood. Explicit Windows recovery step added to CI and actionlint 1.7.12 accepted the workflow. This enforces the missing host-specific evidence instead of assuming Linux coverage proves Windows behavior."
  "2026-09-04T21:13:12.359Z","harness:codex","Review limitation: local Greptile gate returned skipped=true, reason=greptile free review quota exhausted. This is not approval and does not replace hosted reviews. Requested @greptileai on PR #1194. Existing review-loop helper is awaiting checks to terminal before the full comments/reviews/threads/reaction inventory; the Windows enforcement change is held for the consolidated next-head update."
  "2026-09-04T21:18:32.063Z","harness:codex","First hosted head 4c80eb3 completed: only static failed, because npm unpacked size 20024676 exceeded the unchanged 20000000-byte ceiling. Reduce distribution representation of the 1.99 MB SDK manifest without dropping its contract or increasing the ceiling. Sourcery guide also identified missing id/path/zero-length shape diagnostics; existing health integrity scanners already enumerate parse failures and invalid JSON, so verify those with a real fixture before adding redundant health logic."
  "2026-09-04T21:22:13.330Z","harness:codex","TDD review controls: the precise shape-error context and compact-manifest fixture initially failed (4 failures), then all 27 focused tests passed after implementation. A real zero-byte item plus NUL-tail fixture proves existing health --check-only already reports integrity_item_parse_failed:<path> and integrity_history_invalid_json:<id>:L2 without changing either file. No duplicate health scanner was added. Public SDK errors now carry item_id, item_path, byte_length and empty; CLI messages name the item, path and zero-length condition."
  "2026-09-04T21:26:48.011Z","harness:codex","Hosted review availability for initial head: Cubic check is neutral because monthly quota is exhausted; Sourcery code review is skipped because its 7-day diff-character quota is exhausted. Their quota responses are limitations, not approvals. All initial bot comments/review surfaces were read, individually reacted to and acknowledged through scripts/reviews/pr-review-loop.mjs; the Sourcery guide diagnostic feedback is implemented or proven already covered. CodeRabbit full review was explicitly requested after automatic review skipped."
  "2026-09-04T21:37:05.294Z","harness:codex","Review documentation scope: CodeRabbit requested docstrings on touched helpers. Added semantic documentation to nine previously undocumented function declarations whose implementations changed in this delivery. Live pm-4ak1 defines the completed mandatory scope as module documentation, exported declarations, exported data-contract members and public class members; non-exported private helpers are explicitly outside that historical gate. This delivery preserves that 100% public-contract gate and does not mislabel it as universal private-helper documentation."
  "2026-09-04T21:41:25.480Z","harness:codex","Pre-push operational proof: required-mode Sentry and telemetry gate passed on 2026-09-04. Sentry access succeeded over the 14-day window with zero critical/high relevant issues. Telemetry query succeeded with 1.25 percent finish error rate and zero failure rows missing error codes. This is a current health check, not proof that the unmerged branch has been published or that the final local queue is drained."
  "2026-09-04T21:45:39.832Z","harness:codex","Security refresh before the consolidated review update: pnpm security:scan passed; pnpm audit reported zero info/low/moderate/high/critical vulnerabilities across 425 dependencies. Fully paginated GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning open-alert inventories each returned zero. No security threshold, artifact limit or analyzer policy was relaxed."
  "2026-09-04T21:56:16.150Z","harness:codex","Live telemetry freshness proof at 21:55 UTC: the production aggregate query returned latest_event_at 2026-09-04T21:54:32.269Z and 173 events within the preceding 15 minutes. Only aggregate timestamps/counts were read. Final queue drainage is intentionally deferred until after the last operational PM command."
  "2026-09-04T21:58:04.987Z","harness:codex","Review update for PR #1194: all 8397 tests across 605 files passed with exact 100/100/100/100 coverage. Full static quality and typecheck passed. Real temporary-tracker acceptance and packed npm/npx/bunx smoke passed. The package remains below its unchanged 20 MB artifact budget by compacting only the distributed JSON manifest; its documented export and parsed data are unchanged. Required Windows CI now executes both history regression suites. CodeRabbit findings are addressed by a metadata-only existence probe, reuse of the verified salvage hash epoch and an explicit identity-aware validation ok flag. Corrupt-item SDK errors now include item ID/path/byte length/empty state, and the real read-only health regression diagnoses both the zero-byte item and corrupt history tail. Hosted final-head checks and renewed bot review remain required before merge; no publication claim is made."
